Pins the grid repeat literals to f32.

length() and fr() are generic over Into<f32>, so the bare 0.0 and 1.0 only
compile through the f32 fallback that rustc now warns about as a future
hard error (rust-lang/rust#154024). Typing them keeps the build quiet and
keeps it building once the fallback goes.

Diffed against the tree with every earlier patch applied.

--- a/src/taffy.rs
+++ b/src/taffy.rs
@@ -309,7 +309,7 @@
             unit: &Option<u16>,
         ) -> Vec<taffy::GridTemplateComponent<T>> {
             // grid-template-columns: repeat(<number>, minmax(0, 1fr));
-            unit.map(|count| vec![repeat(count, vec![minmax(length(0.0), fr(1.0))])])
+            unit.map(|count| vec![repeat(count, vec![minmax(length(0.0_f32), fr(1.0_f32))])])
                 .unwrap_or_default()
         }
 
